**Short Story:**  
Zizzik the Gnome Warlock tiptoed through Stranglethorn’s jungle, his Succubus, Lash’lora, slinking beside him. A pack of panthers eyed them hungrily. "Seduce that one!" he hissed. Lash’lora obeyed, leaving the others to pounce. Zizzik panicked, frantically draining life as claws raked his robes. "Why didn’t you *taunt*?!" he wheezed. Lash’lora smirked. "Darling, I reduce threat—not invite it." A Voidwalker would’ve tanked the hits, but Zizzik had chosen style over survival. Again.  

**Answer:**  
Voidwalkers are more common because they’re beginner-friendly—reliable taunts and survivability reduce Warlock deaths, especially for less experienced players. Succubus requires active management (CC, threat control) and is squishier, making her better for skilled players but riskier for most. The Voidwalker’s passive safety net appeals to the average player. [end of text]


